#: R/interrater.b.R
msgid ""
"Reliability was assessed via two ICC forms and Krippendorff's interval α on "
"the same {k} raters and {n} cases. ICC (consistency) asks whether raters "
"RANK cases similarly, tolerating a rater who is systematically higher or "
"lower than the others; ICC (absolute agreement) additionally requires their "
"raw VALUES to be interchangeable (Shrout &amp; Fleiss, 1979)."
msgstr ""
"La confiabilidad se evaluó mediante dos formas de ICC y el α de intervalo de "
"Krippendorff sobre los mismos {k} jueces y {n} casos. El ICC (consistencia) "
"pregunta si los jueces ORDENAN los casos de forma similar, tolerando un juez "
"sistemáticamente más alto o más bajo que los demás; el ICC (acuerdo "
"absoluto) exige además que sus VALORES brutos sean intercambiables (Shrout "
"&amp; Fleiss, 1979)."

#: R/advancedreliability.b.R
msgid ""
"Reliability-due-to-G is a substantial share of each factor's own CR/ω -- the "
"general-factor structure captures most of what each subscale reliably "
"measures."
msgstr ""
"La confiabilidad-debida-a-G es una parte sustancial del propio CR/ω de cada "
"factor -- la estructura de factor general captura la mayor parte de lo que "
"cada subescala mide de forma confiable."

